      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm working on a 12 week hypertrophy block for a client but they've completely stalled on their squat for the last 3 weeks. progress just stopped. can you explain how deloading or changing the volume/intensity might help them break through this plateau from a physiological standpoint?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Deloading can help your client recover from accumulated fatigue and rep stress, reducing the risk of overtraining and injury. This process can also encourage muscle recovery, allowing for improved performance and strength gains on subsequent workouts. Additionally, adjusting the volume or intensity by focusing on higher reps within a rep range or modifying accessory exercises may stimulate the muscles differently and help overcome the plateau. By preventing the body from adapting to the same stimulus, your client can break through the stagnation and develop their hypertrophy further.",
